  <div class="prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Wand</p>
    <h1>Wand and lance fittings</h1>
    <Answer>
      There are two ends. The gun end is often M22 or a built-in QC. The tip end is usually 1/4″ QC on anything sold in the last decade.
    </Answer>
    <p>Replacement “20° lances” that will not thread into a big-box gun are usually 1/4″ NPT standing in for an M22 gun outlet, or the reverse. Do not chase it with a pipe wrench. Measure, then use one adapter.</p>
    <p>If the wand is plastic and the coupler is brass, the plastic hex is the part that rounds off. Replace the wand before you ruin the gun outlet.</p>
    <p><a href="/nozzles/">Tips</a> · <a href="/foam-cannon/">Foam cannons</a> · <a href="/surface-cleaner/">Surface cleaners</a></p>
